# Hamilton project configuration. `key=value` per line; `#` starts a comment;
# the value is the literal text after the first `=`.
#
# test_command  the test suite, run from the project root by `hamilton verify`.
#               Must exit 0 on success. Use `python -m pytest`, not bare
#               `pytest`, so the project root is importable from the tests.
# paths.<method>  space-separated dirs holding the tests for one verification
#               method defined in `## Verification methods` in
#               spec/requirements.md, e.g. `paths.browser=tests/browser`. A
#               `@covers` tag counts for an AC only under the paths of one of
#               its methods. `manual` needs no paths.
# run.<method>  a command that runs the test files of that method given to it
#               as arguments, starting whatever they need, e.g.
#               `run.unit=python -m pytest -q`. `hamilton verify R-nnnn/ACn`
#               runs one criterion's tests with it instead of the suite.
#               Which framework runs and where each method's tests live are
#               build-time calls, so `test_command` and the `paths.*` and
#               `run.*` keys are the keys the agent MAY edit during a `build`
#               session.
# model.<step>  which model a kind of build work runs on: `plan`, `tests`,
#               `review`, `code` or `clarify`, e.g. `model.code=opus`. Unset,
#               test writing and review run on a mid-tier model and the rest
#               on the agent's default.
# mutation_command  RESERVED. Per-language mutation testing (see concept.md
#               5.3). Not implemented yet -- if you set it, `hamilton verify`
#               prints a notice every run and does NOT run it. Leave it unset.

test_command=
